{"nodes": [{"id": "craft_docs_configuration_doc", "label": "Craft Configuration Guide", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "Craft/docs/configuration.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "craft_docs_configuration_craftsettings_cs", "label": "Services/CraftSettings.cs", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "Craft/docs/configuration.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "craft_docs_configuration_appsettings_example_jsonc", "label": "appsettings.example.jsonc", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "Craft/docs/configuration.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "craft_docs_configuration_configuration_hierarchy", "label": "Configuration Hierarchy", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "Craft/docs/configuration.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "craft_docs_configuration_roles", "label": "Roles (split deployments)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "Craft/docs/configuration.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "one image can run in split roles (Frontend/Http/Background) selected at runtime, so the cheap-to-scale static frontend and the compute-heavy PowerShell backend can be deployed and scaled independently"}, {"id": "craft_docs_configuration_orchestration_caveat", "label": "Orchestration trigger/process caveat", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "Craft/docs/configuration.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "triggering an orchestration and processing it must happen in the same process - the trigger is an in-process queue, not a durable cross-process one. a pure http node that triggers orchestrations will not run them; must also carry the Background role (backend or combined)"}, {"id": "craft_docs_configuration_worker", "label": "Worker (PowerShell runspace pools)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "Craft/docs/configuration.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "craft_docs_configuration_reuse_runspace_thread", "label": "ReuseRunspaceThread", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "Craft/docs/configuration.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "runs each worker's PowerShell pipeline on one reused thread instead of a new thread per invocation; the biggest single per-request dispatch win (~50% of PS-invoke cost, +68% throughput on dispatch-bound load per docs/dispatch-analysis.md), matches the Azure Functions PS worker's persistent runspace"}, {"id": "craft_docs_configuration_auth", "label": "Auth settings", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "Craft/docs/configuration.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "craft_docs_configuration_scheduler", "label": "Scheduler (cron background tasks)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "Craft/docs/configuration.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "craft_docs_configuration_background_concurrency_limiter", "label": "Background concurrency limiter", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "Craft/docs/configuration.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "craft_docs_configuration_orchestrator", "label": "Orchestrator (fan-out/fan-in)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "Craft/docs/configuration.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "batches/coalesces per-task status writes off the fan-out critical path in <=100-entity byte-budgeted Azure Table transactions (the throughput fix for large fan-outs, per docs/orch-analysis.md); the pre-invoke Running marker is persisted under a durable barrier by default so AttemptCount/MaxRetries still bounds poison tasks"}, {"id": "craft_docs_configuration_cache", "label": "Cache (response cache)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "Craft/docs/configuration.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "craft_docs_configuration_cache_admission_policy", "label": "Cache admission policy", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "Craft/docs/configuration.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "a response is cached only when the handler is a side-effect-free GET List* read AND the request passes ordered gates (ExcludedEndpoints, NoCacheHeader, RequiredParam missing/blank/excluded); a bypassed request never reads or writes the cache so it can't collide with a differently-scoped entry"}, {"id": "craft_docs_configuration_scripts", "label": "Scripts (module discovery)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "Craft/docs/configuration.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "craft_docs_configuration_native_endpoints", "label": "Native C# endpoints and scheduled tasks", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "Craft/docs/configuration.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "craft_docs_configuration_central_handler", "label": "ICraftEndpointHandler central dispatch", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "Craft/docs/configuration.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "the native counterpart of Scripts:HttpHandler - one place every authenticated API call funnels through; Dispatch defaults to Central so a route that never thought about it gets the application's authorization rather than becoming accidentally public. Direct routes are logged at startup as the security-review checklist"}, {"id": "craft_docs_configuration_realtime", "label": "Realtime (SSE)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "Craft/docs/configuration.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "craft_docs_configuration_realtime_bridge_plan_doc", "label": "realtime-bridge-plan.md", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "Craft/docs/configuration.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "craft_docs_configuration_frontend_csp", "label": "Frontend Content-Security-Policy", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "Craft/docs/configuration.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "EasyAuth handles auth/redirects/excluded paths at the platform layer; Craft only adds response headers EasyAuth doesn't touch (CSP). keep 'self' in default-src and connect-src or same-origin fetch breaks over http; keep data: in connect-src for emscripten SINGLE_FILE wasm builds that fetch a base64 data: URL"}, {"id": "craft_docs_configuration_env_vars", "label": "Environment Variables (process-level)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "Craft/docs/configuration.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "craft_docs_configuration_auth_env_vars", "label": "Authentication Environment Variables", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "Craft/docs/configuration.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "craft_docs_configuration_ke